{
  "description": "Cases every runtime reads through the shared LiNo front end (js/src/rml-lino-frontend.mjs and rust/src/lino_frontend.rs). A source is a string, or a list of strings and {\"repeat\", \"times\"} parts joined in order. A case expects either \"forms\" (the text, 1-based line, code-point column, and length of every top-level form) or an E006 \"error\"; \"prepared\", \"lines\" (the [line, column] of every logical line), and \"quotes\" (the [line, column, text, value] of every reference that starts with a quote: where it starts, the source text it spans, and the reference it reads as) are what the prepare step returns, and a case without them expects the prepare step to fail with the same error. The prepare step puts a space in place of each UTF-16 code unit it blanks in JavaScript and of each UTF-8 byte in Rust, so every character a case blanks is ASCII.",
